--- Count-to-Infinity on X-Y-Z (cost=1 each, Y-Z fails) ---
  Round 1: Y->Z =  3, X->Z =  2 (counting to infinity!)
  Round 2: Y->Z =  3, X->Z =  4 (counting to infinity!)
  Round 3: Y->Z =  5, X->Z =  4 (counting to infinity!)
  Round 4: Y->Z =  5, X->Z =  6 (counting to infinity!)
  Round 5: Y->Z =  7, X->Z =  6 (counting to infinity!)
  Round 6: Y->Z =  7, X->Z =  8 (counting to infinity!)
  With Split Horizon + Poison Reverse: X advertises Z=INF (16 in RIP) back to Y -> Y immediately sets Y->Z=INF in Round 1!

--- Alternative Concept Analysis: Link-State (OSPF) vs Distance-Vector on C-D Failure ---
  - Link-State: C and D flood 1 LSA each across 6 links (~12 LSA messages), every router recomputes SPF in 1 flood + 1 Dijkstra (~ms).
  - Distance-Vector: Exchanges full vectors with neighbours over multiple rounds (and risks count-to-infinity without poison reverse).
